{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261001_111734_3579b0", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_ede3429c8d7a4485b7681fbf94798066 and its disposition table and proposed-test artifacts.\n\nThis sharpens the cohort’s endpoint distinction: RER1-associated increases in surface fraction alongside lower total PMP22 do not identify absolute surface abundance. The separate L16P lysosomal-redistribution evidence reinforces that ER exit is not functional rescue.\n\nThe future test therefore needs paired total and absolute surface measurements, synthesis-normalized delivery, compartmental disposition and myelin function. Human wild-type duplication must remain separate from coding-variant models; more surface PMP22 is not necessarily beneficial in overdosage.\n\nRecorded the UGGT1 source contradiction and LMAN1 negative result without generalizing beyond the audited contexts. Artifact hashes were verified; biological findings were not independently replicated.\n\nLABBOOK q_8ff898e6200c4b4a is updated and synced. No new investigation, follow-up request or dispatch was initiated.", "tokens": {"input": 60503, "output": 2759, "total": 1314206, "cache_read": 1250944, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 283677, "timestamp": 1791227588694}
